1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,874
A blister?

2
00:00:00,874 --> 00:00:01,997
Should you pop it?

3
00:00:01,997 --> 00:00:02,746
Usually, no.

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:06,813
Step one.

5
00:00:06,813 --> 00:00:07,751
Leave it alone.

6
00:00:07,751 --> 00:00:12,629
The skin on top protects the new skin underneath, and helps prevent infection.

7
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:13,848
Step two.

8
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:17,874
Cover it with a loose dressing or a padded plaster, so it doesn't rub.

9
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:19,908
Step three.

10
00:00:19,908 --> 00:00:24,322
If it bursts, wash it with clean water, leave the loose skin in place, and cover it.

11
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:26,914
Step four.

12
00:00:26,914 --> 00:00:27,907
Cut the friction.

13
00:00:27,907 --> 00:00:29,893
Wear well-fitting shoes and socks.

14
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:36,051
Pus, spreading redness, more pain or swelling, or a fever?

15
00:00:36,051 --> 00:00:36,884
See a doctor.

16
00:00:36,884 --> 00:00:41,631
Also see one if you have diabetes, or the blister is large or from a burn.
